---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/logs.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engineering Logs — Oreslang"
  description="Oreslang engineering logs about compiler architecture, actors, runtime isolation, LLVM, GraalVM, AOT and JIT."
>
  <section class="page-hero log-index-hero">
    <p class="kicker">Field notes from the compiler</p>
    <h1>Engineering logs.</h1>
    <p>Decisions, tradeoffs, and works in progress from the Oreslang language and runtime.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-body log-index-body" aria-label="Published engineering logs">
    <ol class="log-list">
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/6/" aria-label="Read log 6: Actor-native LLM architectures"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 006</span><h2>Actor-native LLM architectures: building neural networks with Oreslang</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>Actor-managed Transformers and MoE, typed forward/backward pipelines, GPU tensor kernels, persistent neural memory, and a measurable implementation roadmap.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/5/" aria-label="Read log 5: How to market open-source software"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 005</span><h2>How to market open-source software: an engineering-first playbook</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>An engineering-first marketing guide, expanded with AEO for programming languages: how LLMs encounter code, versioned Oreslang references, agent instructions, MCP, and compiler-tested AI generation.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-13">October 13, 2026</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/4/" aria-label="Read log 4: Oreslang style guide"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 004</span><h2>Oreslang style guide: names, formatting, and actor boundaries</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>snake_case callables, CamelCase everywhere else, one canonical formatter, optional semicolons, and explicit actor ownership, lifecycle, and recovery conventions.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-12">October 12, 2026</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/3/" aria-label="Read log 3: Actors for AI/ML and data pipelines"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 003</span><h2>Actors for AI/ML and data pipelines</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>Warm model workers, bounded CPU/GPU pipelines, tensor ownership, HPC scheduling and supervised agent fleets with multi-party authorization.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-12">October 12, 2026</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/2/" aria-label="Read log 2: Oreslang across browsers, mobile, edge and embedded environments"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 002</span><h2>Beyond GraalVM and LLVM: one Oreslang, every environment</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>Wasm, WASI, JavaScript, Android DEX, native AOT and embedded runtimes—and source headers that let the compiler reject incompatible imports and undeclared capabilities.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-10">October 10, 2026</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
      <li>
        <article class="log-list-entry">
          <a href="/logs/1/" aria-label="Read log 1: LLVM versus GraalVM"><span class="log-entry-number">Log 001</span><h2>LLVM vs. GraalVM: one Oreslang, two AOT backends</h2><span class="log-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <p>What's missing, what belongs in a native LLVM runtime, what should stay in the managed Graal/JVM world, and how to make both truly AOT-capable with optional JIT.</p>
          <p class="log-list-meta"><span>Alex Mills</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-08T21:04:00Z">October 8, 2026 · 21:04 UTC</time></p>
        </article>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
